Thanks Colin.<br><br>You are correct - „2 Lines“ or „Auto“ is/was set on both RD5R and also on most of my other devices. <br><br>I just compared the GD77 display to the RD5R and the “issue creating contacts” show up nicely with the „line below the line“ on a GD77 – yet that content probably creates the „few pixels“ on the RD5R. My assumption was that this is always cropped based on TRX capabilities, no matter how many chars are in contacts/DB or via TA (while being created in mem and before transferring to the actual display). <br><br>As it seems the RD5R can cope with a total of 25 chars for callsign plus additional info without showing any additional pixels. One of the RD5R is currently configured with „2 Lines“ and callsign database write parameters limited to these 25 chars to check if CC issue shows up again. The other RD5R is set to “1 Line” for now.<br><br>I’ll continue with some testing and provide further details once the “candidates” with the longer DB/TA details show up again…<br><br>Cheers<br>—Michael<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2090">DG1GMY</a> — Thu Dec 29, 2022 12:56 pm</p><hr />
